---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import LegalDocument from "../components/LegalDocument.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy — Filosign"
	description="How Filosign handles personal data for document signing and optional payment features."
>
	<div
		class="min-h-screen bg-background font-manrope selection:bg-primary/10 selection:text-primary"
	>
		<Navbar />
		<main>
			<LegalDocument
				title="Privacy Policy"
				description="This policy describes data Filosign processes when you use our applications. It is not legal advice."
				lastUpdated="May 2026"
			>
				<h2>1. What we process</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						Account and profile data (for example email, wallet address, display
						name) to operate signing workflows.
					</li>
					<li>
						Document metadata, participant information, and encrypted document
						content according to product design.
					</li>
					<li>
						When you attach optional USDC payouts through Filosign: payout
						amounts, token and validator addresses, on-chain rule identifiers,
						transaction hashes, and status fields used for UI and compliance
						exports.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>2. On-chain data</h2>
				<p>
					Blockchain transactions you sign (including <code>registerRule</code>
					and <code>approve</code>) are public on the network. Filosign does not
					control public chain data. Rules created without the Filosign app are
					not indexed by us unless they are later associated through a supported
					send flow.
				</p>

				<h2>3. Third parties</h2>
				<p>
					We may use infrastructure and service providers (hosting, email,
					analytics, wallet authentication, and optional automated payout relay).
					Their processing is limited to operating Filosign.
				</p>

				<h2>4. Payments disclaimer</h2>
				<p>
					Filosign does not control or screen all on-chain payouts. Payment
					status shown in the product reflects our indexing of the supported send
					path where applicable, not a complete view of all activity on public
					contracts.
				</p>

				<p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground pt-6">
					See our <a href="/terms" class="underline">Terms of Service</a> for
					payment and non-custody terms.
				</p>
			</LegalDocument>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
